+## Broadcom rendering bandwidth
+
+Fractional video scaling uses bilinear sampling on Broadcom. Uncropped frames
+combine color conversion and scaling directly into the output; cropped frames
+use the existing bilinear blit. Output resolution, aspect ratio, and crop remain
+unchanged. Other GPUs retain the high-order filter ladder.
+
+The console omits progressive backdrop blur and scroll fade layers on Broadcom.
+Scroll contents remain clipped to their viewport, with text at native resolution.
+Opaque console frames replace the entire output without clearing or blending an
+underlying picture. Transparent streaming overlays retain their existing path.
+The kiosk selects an eight-bit SDR swapchain; HDR-to-SDR conversion remains a
+separate workload requiring physical performance checks.
+
+## Kiosk integration
+
+The image builder in `packaging/rpi5/kiosk` supplies Weston, Vulkan, PipeWire,
+Bluetooth, network services, and the matching runtime bundle. The application
+remains usable as a portable bundle on a suitably configured Linux system.
+
+The kiosk uses a patched Weston DRM backend with software cursors. Physical
+testing reproduced compositor restarts while scrolling the home screen with a
+controller. After the cursor fix, three measurements showed stable 60 page flips
+per second and the user confirmed smooth scrolling without further restarts.
+That evidence belongs to the tested image; new builds require fresh acceptance.
+Hardware display planes remain available: disabling the faulty cursor plane does
+not require `WESTON_FORCE_RENDERER`, which also disables efficient scanout paths.
+
+See [fork maintenance](rpi5-fork.md) for build and release checks.
+
+## Rebase and validation checklist
+
+1. Record the old and proposed upstream base commits.
+2. Rebase each downstream commit deliberately; do not silently drop a commit or
+   hunk to make the rebase pass.
+3. Review `git range-diff <old-base>..<old-tip> <new-base>..<new-tip>` and update
+   this rationale if implementation or behavior changed.
+4. Keep the V4L2 Request rung and the pinned Raspberry Pi FFmpeg build compatible.
+5. Run the Rust tests, including the PLC tests, and produce the ARM64 release
+   bundle.
+6. On Pi 5, verify 1920x1080 HEVC reports `v4l2-request`, reaches the first-frame
+   readiness event, and does not fall back to `software`.
+7. Verify physical cadence with statistics both off and on at 60 Hz and another
+   supported mode such as 50 or 120 Hz.
+8. Exercise compositor resize or mode changes and confirm swapchain recreation.
+9. Run a sustained audio test including delayed or stalled delivery. Diagnose
+   PipeWire/HDMI health separately from Punktfunk packet reconciliation.
+10. Record the upstream base, fork commit/tag, Pi revision, image identifier,
+    display mode, codec, and relevant log evidence with the release.
+
+Temporary experiments that did not form part of the validated solution—such as
+disabling the overlay entirely or adding a separate source-clock pacing branch—
+are intentionally absent and should not be restored merely to ease a rebase.
